WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.557
The CTE first creates one row per product, category, and month.

00:00:04.557 --> 00:00:08.892
The outer query then groups by category and creates month columns.

00:00:08.892 --> 00:00:11.172
So there are two grain changes.

00:00:11.172 --> 00:00:13.757
Run the query and state both of them.

00:00:13.757 --> 00:00:20.537
Being explicit about intermediate grain is one of the best protections against accidental double counting.

00:00:20.537 --> 00:00:25.237
Joining detail tables before reshaping can multiply rows.

00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:30.602
If the target is one row per patient or product, summarize each one-to-many source to the target grain

00:00:30.602 --> 00:00:33.232
before combining them.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:38.669
This keeps measures interpretable and prevents a pivot from hiding earlier join inflation.
